# 000725.SZ — BOE Technology Group | Full investment artifact

**Research date:** 17 September 2026 | **Framework:** 6.0 consolidated | **Format:** standalone current-state analysis
**Status:** New standalone screen; no original artifact was available | **Classification:** BENEFICIARY — display scale; speculative glass-substrate option
**Artifact Base:** 32/60 = **53% — Fail** | **Protected portfolio Base:** 65% (user override retained; separate from artifact assessment)
**Snapshot:** supplied-workbook price CNY 6.070; model share proxy 37,044.328064M; implied snapshot market capitalization 224,859.071 CNY millions. Price is frozen from the supplied workbook, not a current-market refresh; capitalization uses the modeled denominator.
**Active ceiling:** Q3 2027 **CNY 7.552825**, pricing Q3 2027–Q2 2028. All 15 quarterly ceilings are derived below.

BOE has a credible path to more OLED content and a separate glass-processing opportunity. Display economics dominate this valuation through 2030. The glass substrate pathway is included as probability-weighted optionality, with the required capacity, sellable yield and price assumptions exposed.

## 1. Supercycle, supply chain and durable advantage

BOE is a large display producer with related manufacturing and glass-processing capabilities. OLED penetration and declining legacy depreciation can improve display economics. Glass-core substrates provide a distinct emerging opportunity, but pilot qualification is not proof of high-volume orders or supply-chain exclusivity. This new artifact uses the existing workbook only as the before baseline; the unavailable original narrative has not been reconstructed or assumed.

Display devices: terminal demand → screen area, technology and product mix → LCD/OLED fabrication, module assembly and customer qualification. Emerging packaging: large compute packages → glass-core substrate specifications → TGV, copper fill, redistribution and multilayer build-up → qualified substrate sales. BOE can reuse glass-processing and manufacturing capabilities, but this does not establish an irreplaceable AI chokepoint. Glass core, glass interposer and temporary carrier are different products.

| Business / curve | Stage | Evidence and next inflection |
| --- | --- | --- |
| LCD displays | Mature/peak qualitative band | Cyclical price and utilization matter more than an unconstrained market narrative. |
| IT/automotive OLED | Early commercial ramp | Higher penetration expands content beyond smartphone panels. |
| Glass-core packaging | Pre-ramp 0–10% | Pilot and customer technical tests precede serial production. |
| MicroLED optical interconnect | Research stage | No commercial revenue or production schedule is established. |

Stage percentages are qualitative framework bands relative to a possible mature opportunity, not measured market penetration. A current capacity constraint can coexist with a larger long-term TAM; qualification and economic capture decide how much reaches this company.

## 2. Forward TAM and the three-phase expansion lens

| Phase | Engineering opportunity | Demand-to-company bridge |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Phase 1;100% thematic | Large-area displays and current OLED | Screen size, replacement and premium mix determine the sold-area wallet. Industry demand softness remains relevant despite a larger long-term opportunity. |
| Phase 2;50% thematic | OLED IT/automotive and advanced substrates | OLED2027 sales 58B→203087B CNY require 1.5×recognized revenue. Illustratively 1.6×premium area/units ×0.9375 net ASP/mix gives that path. This is a demand-capture scenario, not a disclosed shipment forecast. |
| Phase 3;20% thematic | Glass-core packaging, optical interconnect and adjacent energy technology | Glass enables different dimensional stability and packaging architectures. The model sizes panels actually sellable under stated capacity, utilization and ASP assumptions; it does not assign BOE the entire AI-packaging TAM. Optical interconnect and perovskite research have no additional dollar layer. |

The 100% / 50% / 20% thematic weights guide thesis assessment. They are not blanket discounts to reported sales, contracts or all forecasts. Programme probabilities below govern only separately identified optionality. Current reported sales calibrate the starting point; they do not cap the future market.

## 3. Current earnings and management evidence

H1 2026 revenue was CNY 103,132.383M and cost of sales CNY 87,629.902M, implying GP CNY 15,502.480M. Reported operating profit was CNY 7,262.818M and parent net income CNY 5,247.660M. Reported OP includes other/investment/fair-value income and finance costs; the recurring manufacturing bridge below is different. Total A+B shares were 37,044.328064M at June 30.

Both September 10 company-written investor Q&A records (042 and 043), published September 11, were read in full. They are written management disclosures, not audio-call transcripts. The half-year results provide the accounting anchor. No complete half-year earnings-call transcript was obtained.

The two newest company-written September 10 Q&A records were read in full during this research, together with the half-year financial report and June production record. These are written disclosures, not two audio earnings transcripts. No complete half-year call was obtained. BOE’s original narrative was absent, so the supplied workbook alone supplies the before values.

## 4. Local evidence and calibration packet

Chinese-language written management Q&A supplies the five variables: TAM through new IT OLED and glass applications; demand through current display conditions; margin through yield/depreciation; timing through qualification and factory ramps; risk through lack of mass glass orders and ownership structure. H1 GP 15,502.480M less 12,438.079M sales/admin/R&D/taxes/impairments gives 3,064.402M core OP. This excludes financing and non-operating income and is not the 7,262.818M statutory OP. The July increase in Hefei ownership changes parent participation in already consolidated economics; it does not create an equal increase in consolidated sales.

## 5. Summing thesis score

| Category | Points / maximum | Evidence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Core Thesis | 11/20 | Display scale and process capabilities; no proven mandatory AI supply-chain position. |
| Cycle | 5/10 | Latest management discussion describes weak Q3 display demand and price stabilization. |
| TAM | 8/10 | OLED IT/automotive and glass-core substrates expand opportunity, with qualification gates. |
| Catalysts | 3/5 | OLED line ramp and pilot qualification; mass glass revenue not yet confirmed. |
| Macro | 7/10 | Display replacement and OLED adoption, tempered by consumer demand and memory-cost pressure. |
| Alpha | 3/5 | Glass capability is tangible, but earnings attribution remains small at pilot scale. |
| Risks | -5 | Display pricing, OLED execution, glass commercialization, capital/minority economics and recurring-profit quality; one deduction per independent class. |

**Sum: 32/60 × 100 = 53.333333%, conventionally rounded to 53%.** This advisory thesis score does not replace any portfolio Base override. The separate risk classes below total the displayed deduction; holding status and classification do not waive that deduction.

## 6. Revenue sources, capture and product margins

Calendar quarters; preserve the workbook’s 20× OP multiple for comparability. H1 core operating bridge: GP minus sales 988.067, admin 3,005.196, R&D 6,768.051, business taxes 741.056, credit impairment 25.478 and asset impairment 910.230 (CNY M), giving core OP about CNY 3,064.402M. Exclude financing, subsidies/other income, investment returns and fair-value/disposal gains; do not call this reported statutory OP. Q3/Q4 are forecasts. Start from H1 revenue/2; allocate display 70% LCD and 30% OLED as an undisclosed analyst split. Other consolidated businesses include IoT, MLED, sensors, healthcare and eliminations; their net margin is a reconciliation proxy. Annual LCD/OLED/other revenue in 2027–30 is [117/58/47], [120/68/51.5], [124/78/56], [127/87/60] CNY billions. Seasonality is 22/24/26/28%. Product GP captures the explicit margin/yield assumptions; operating cost plus impairment allowance falls from the H1 rate to 11.5/11/10.5/10% in 2027–30. No depreciation add-back. Glass revenue equals panels per month × 3 × sellable utilization × assumed ASP: 2027 1,000 panels, 25/40/60/70%, CNY 5,000; 2028 2/3/4/5 thousand panels, 65%, CNY 5,500; 2029 8/10/12/14 thousand, 75%, CNY 5,750; 2030 16/18/20/22 thousand, 85%, CNY 6,000. Expansion above 1,000/month and all ASPs/utilization are unsupported conditional assumptions requiring new funding and qualification. The glass helper uses a CNY 1M unit anchor with revenue-equivalent factors, not an observed sale. Glass is carved out as future incremental packaging revenue; no separate CPO or perovskite windfall is added. Denominator includes all issued A+B shares, including restricted shares, at 37,044.328064M; no future buyback cancellation credit. Additional option dilution is not fully quantified. Consolidated core OP is the preserved framework convention and is not parent-attributable earnings; minority interests are a material valuation limitation. Glass is separate unproven optionality: all displayed glass revenue factors are multiplied by 50% commercialization probability. Thus 2027 gross scenario 29.25M becomes 14.625M included sales;2030 gross scenario 1,162.8M becomes 581.4M. Probability is applied once to revenue and related product GP; it is not a claim that half of a physical panel is sold. Existing corporate R&D and impairment allowances remain in operating costs and are not probability-discounted. Scores use the framework maximum 5-point risk deduction, combining capital and minority-ownership exposure in one economic-claim class.

| Vector | Actual calibration / source | Forward demand and capture | Margin derivation / constraint |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| LCD | 70% undisclosed allocation of H1 display revenue; Q3 price/demand adjustment already in anchor. | Annual 117/120/124/127B CNY 2027–30;1.08547×growth can be decomposed illustratively into 1.10×sold area ×0.98656 netprice/mix. This is a mild recovery case, not an AI-rate extrapolation. | 16%→17% product GM assumes utilization and lower legacy depreciation outweigh price pressure. Depreciation remains in COGS. |
| OLED | 30% historical display allocation; not reported segment actual. | Annual 58/68/78/87B CNY; broader IT/automotive penetration supports 1.5×revenue 2027→30, while product ASP erosion is allowed in the illustrative bridge. | 13%→22% GM is a conditional yield/loading improvement. It is not current guidance; new-line depreciation can delay it. |
| Other consolidated businesses | H1 net revenue 21,376.945M and GP 5,081.958M after eliminations. | Annual 47/51.5/56/60B includes IoT, MLED, sensors and healthcare. No separate full market forecast is added to this residual. | 23% net GP proxy; changing business mix and intercompany transactions can change this rate. |
| Glass-core optionality | Issuer pilot design 1,000 panels/month; no verified mass-sales base. | Gross revenue=monthly panels×3×sellable utilization×ASP.2027 at 1,000/month,25/40/60/70% and 5,000 CNY gives 29.25M gross,14.625M at 50% probability.2030 at 16/18/20/22k/month,85% and 6,000 CNY gives 1,162.8M gross,581.4M included. Expansion and ASP are assumptions. | 10% 2027→30% 2030 conditional GM after manufacturing costs. Probability weights revenue/GP once; corporate R&D is not discounted. At 5,000 CNY and 10% GM, unitcost 4,500 CNY is the implied viability requirement. |

**Confidence:** reported historical totals are HIGH. Source-based forward extrapolations are MEDIUM only where the cited source sizes the relevant period; other product allocations, future capture and margin assumptions are LOW. A source for the historical anchor does not make an unsourced future factor management guidance. The detailed factors below are the single modeled base case, with uncertain assumptions exposed for review.

### V1. LCD display (estimated split)

Sources: B1/2;70% historical display split, price/area forecast. Revenue = anchor × factor; GP/contribution = revenue × displayed product margin. Forecast confidence: LOW unless a specific actual/guided total is identified above.

| Quarter | Revenue anchor | Demand / conversion factor | Revenue | Product margin | GP / contribution |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Q3 2026 | 28,042.115066 | 1.000000 | 28,042.115 | 14.000% | 3,925.896 |
| Q4 2026 | 28,042.115066 | 1.030612 | 28,900.547 | 15.000% | 4,335.082 |
| Q1 2027 | 28,042.115066 | 0.917905 | 25,740.000 | 16.000% | 4,118.400 |
| Q2 2027 | 28,042.115066 | 1.001351 | 28,080.000 | 16.000% | 4,492.800 |
