## 10. Annual trajectory cross-check

| Calendar year | Revenue | GP / contribution | Opex | OP | OP margin |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 2027 | 222,014.625 | 37,071.463 | 25,531.682 | 11,539.781 | 5.198% |
| 2028 | 239,575.075 | 43,220.015 | 26,353.258 | 16,866.757 | 7.040% |
| 2029 | 258,284.625 | 49,631.156 | 27,119.886 | 22,511.271 | 8.716% |
| 2030 | 274,581.400 | 54,704.420 | 27,458.140 | 27,246.280 | 9.923% |

These are calendar-year sums of the quarterly path, not extra revenue and not the live valuation method. For non-December fiscal reporters, fiscal guidance and these calendar totals must be aligned using the period mapping above; a four-quarter run rate is not automatically the same fiscal year. Outer-year outputs are conditional TAM/capture trajectories, not verified management sales targets.

2027 conventional sales 222B plus 14.625M weighted glass;2028 conventional 239.5B plus 75.075M;2029 conventional 258B plus 284.625M;2030 conventional 274B plus 581.4M. Glass is only about 0.21% of 2030 modeled consolidated revenue even after a 22×pilot-capacity expansion. That scale check shows why an enlarged glass TAM alone cannot currently justify valuing the entire group as a glass bottleneck. OLED profitability remains the dominant modeled change.

