This isolates denominator uncertainty; it is not a second bull/bear operating case or permission to remove known dilution. The base case remains the explicit share path in the rolling table.

## 12. Programme and probability ledger

| Programme / signal | Source and probability | Amount / unit base | Treatment in this model | Escalation / recognition |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Current LCD/OLED operations | Reported revenue;95% continuation confidence | Historical financial base | No probability discount to reported actuals | Quarterly volume, prices and yield update product mix. |
| IT OLED ramp | Issuer production milestone;75% execution confidence | 8.6-generation line and 58→87B modeled OLED | Embedded sales path; no duplicate new-factory revenue | Customer-qualified output and product margin. |
| Glass-core commercialization | Management technical progress;50% financial-conversion probability | Explicit panels×utilization×ASP gross scenario | Included once at 50%; no additional glass TAM layer | Repeat accepted orders→75–85%; full production→95%; capacity evidence resets units. |
| MicroLED optical/CPO | Research signal;25% commercial confidence | No defensible order/ASP base | Unquantified opportunity, zero separate revenue | Prototype→customer qualification→production economics. |
| Perovskite | Technical development;25% scale confidence | No verified material earnings base | No speculative windfall | Long-duration field results and funded customer orders. |

Probabilities are analyst judgments under the framework signal hierarchy. Embedded revenue is not multiplied or added a second time. Where no defensible amount or unit base exists, the opportunity remains explicitly unquantified; confidence alone cannot create a revenue number. New evidence can enlarge the TAM, improve capture or move recognition earlier, but each requires an identifiable model input.

## 13. Scored risk classes

| Risk class | Scored deduction | Mechanism and consequence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Display pricing cycle | -1 | Weak demand or higher supply can offset larger area shipments and lower depreciation. |
| OLED execution | -1 | Yield, customer qualification and depreciation can delay expected margins. |
| Glass commercialization | -1 | Pilot success does not prove repeat orders, reliable high-volume yield or funded expansion. |
| Capital and minority economics | -1 | Fabs require large investment; non-controlling claims reduce listed shareholders’ share of consolidated economics. |
| Recurring-profit quality | -1 | Investment/fair-value gains can mask weak manufacturing returns; impairments can recur. |

## 14. Dated catalysts, counters and escalation

1. **2026-10-31 monitoring date — Q3 results** Reconcile display pricing, OLED mix and core costs; do not carry investment gains into manufacturing OP.

2. **2026-12-31 — Glass pilot conversion** Identify accepted paid shipments, not only reliability tests.

3. **2027-06-30 — IT OLED output** Track line yield, loading and depreciation against 13% model GM.

4. **2027-12-31 — Glass commercialization** Replace 1,000 panel scenario with actual throughput, sellable yield and ASP.

5. **2028–2030 annual reviews — Expansion and ownership** New capacity requires a funded plan and parent-economic-claim bridge.

6. **Each capital filing — Share denominator** Reconcile A+B shares, cancellations, awards and minority changes.

## 15. Cross-book monitoring

ASE’s packaging demand is an addressable application for glass substrates, not proof of a BOE order. BOE’s Micro-LED interconnect research is not interchangeable with Credo DSP/optics or silicon-photonics foundry revenue. Avoid summing the same packaging substrate, carrier and interposer markets as three BOE revenue pools. Higher memory prices can hurt display terminal affordability while benefiting memory holdings; a common AI narrative does not imply every segment benefits equally. ASE’s changing package requirements may enlarge glass demand, but awarded substrate share and parent economics must still be demonstrated.

## 16. Source register and model limits

**B1 — [BOE H1 report, issuer English version](https://money.finance.sina.com.cn/corp/view/vCB_AllBulletinDetail.php?id=12572089&stockid=000725) (2026-08-29).** Display revenue/COGS: CNY 81,755.438/71,334.915M. Remaining consolidated revenue/GP are CNY 21,376.945/5,081.958M after eliminations. Core cost bridge includes sales/admin/R&D, business taxes and impairments; manufacturing depreciation is already in COGS.

**B2 — [Company investor Q&A 042](https://file.finance.sina.com.cn/211.154.219.97:9494/MRGG/CNSESZ_STOCK/2026/2026-9/2026-09-11/12595879.PDF) (2026-09-10).** Q3 LCD demand is weak; September TV pricing is expected to stabilize. Depreciation and capex are expected to decline from 2025. Hefei ownership rose from 36.67% to 50.14% in July. Repurchased A/B shares are not automatically assumed cancelled in this model.

**B3 — [Company investor Q&A 043](https://file.finance.sina.com.cn/211.154.219.97:9494/MRGG/CNSESZ_STOCK/2026/2026-9/2026-09-11/12595880.PDF) (2026-09-10).** Glass-core substrate pilot design capacity is 1,000 panels/month. Reliability tests and sampling have progressed. BOE distinguishes glass-core substrates from temporary carriers and glass interposers. Micro-LED optical interconnect and glass-substrate CPO remain technical research projects.

**B4 — [AMOLED production milestone, company Q&A](https://static.cninfo.com.cn/finalpage/2026-06-17/1225377171.PDF) (2026-06-17).** The 8.6-generation AMOLED line held its production/customer-delivery ceremony. Commercial output and margins still depend on yield and loading.

No original BOE artifact was supplied; only the before workbook exists. LCD/OLED mix, future margins, glass ASP/yield/expansion, seasonality and other-business net GP are LOW-confidence assumptions. No mass-production glass order or quantified optical-interconnect revenue was verified. Consolidated OP is not adjusted for minority claims or net debt, so the framework ceiling is not a standard equity fair value. Current total shares are a proxy, not a fully reconstructed diluted option schedule.

